<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">21092026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Washington's preparing to sanction the International Criminal Court itself... not just its judges and prosecutors, but the institution, barring most transactions with it after a grace period of several months.</s> <s>Banks that clear dollars tend to over-comply, so the court's payroll and IT purchases could stall, and American citizens would need a Treasury licence to give it money, goods or services.</s> <s>The United States never joined the court, yet it may be able to starve the only permanent war-crimes tribunal, and every victim community with a case before it, without touching its mandate.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Israel's national security minister, Itamar Ben-Gvir, led settlers into the Al-Aqsa compound around Yom Kippur, and his police are the ones who control access to the site.</s> <s>Jordan, the site's custodian under its nineteen ninety-four treaty with Israel, says the entire fourteen-hectare compound is exclusively Muslim and administered only by the Jerusalem Islamic Waqf, and Qatar and Kuwait have joined its condemnation.</s> <s>Each ministerial visit shifts the status quo by precedent rather than decree... while Palestinian worshippers face tightening limits on their own access.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iran says its terms for reopening the Strait of Hormuz have reached Washington through mediators, as Pakistan's interior minister, Mohsin Naqvi, arrives in Tehran for talks.</s> <s>Security chief Mohsen Rezaei named three conditions: an end to the war, the release of frozen funds, and a lifting of the naval blockade.</s> <s>Brent crude still slid to about a hundred and two dollars on hopes for diplomacy at the UN this week, which suggests traders are pricing in a deal, not the strait itself.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Sanaa, Houthi leader Mahdi al-Mashat declared an equation of blockade for blockade against Saudi Arabia, and in the same address assured Washington that American ships in the Red Sea are safe.</s> <s>The trigger was a coalition airstrike on Sanaa airport that stopped a flight carrying a Houthi delegation, and the group now describes its strikes as mirroring more than a decade of air, sea and import restrictions on Yemen.</s> <s>It's the first time since twenty twenty-three that they've treated their two adversaries as separate fights, and Yemenis, who were close to a truce, are the ones who'll pay for it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>On Saint Pierre and Miquelon, the last scrap of France left in North America, Emmanuel Macron backed Canada to become the EU's first associate member.</s> <s>The islands survived the seventeen sixty-three treaty that ended New France, and Mark Carney's visit, the first ever by a Canadian prime minister, came after Donald Trump posted a map draping the American flag over both Canada and the islands.</s> <s>Both governments have told their space agencies and defence ministries to share launch systems, but nobody's yet said what associate membership would mean in trade or law.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Rojava's autonomous administration in northeast Syria formally dissolved on the twenty-fifth of August.</s> <s>A government offensive in January forced the Syrian Democratic Forces to fold into the state under President Ahmed al-Sharaa, ending Kurdish-led self-rule that began in the chaos of twenty twelve.</s> <s>Fadia Ismail, whose son died fighting ISIS, calls it the imposition of defeat, and that's a verdict many families who buried fighters in that war may come to share.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Eighteen suspects in the killing of Haitian President Jovenel Moïse have been flown out of Port-au-Prince on a military flight to face trial in Florida.</s> <s>Prosecutors say the plot was financed and staged in southern Florida, and thirty people have been indicted so far.</s> <s>A president was murdered in his own home, and his accused killers will be tried in a foreign court... which shows how little is left of Haiti's own justice system.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Foreign investors have built a record two hundred and ninety thousand short contracts against Indian index futures.</s> <s>They've also sold nearly twenty-one thousand crore rupees of Indian shares this month, as oil climbed from eighty-two dollars in early August to almost a hundred and four on Friday.</s> <s>India imports most of its crude, so every dollar on Brent widens the current-account deficit and pushes back rate cuts, and foreign money's betting on that chain rather than against Indian companies.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A trade truce between Washington and Beijing expires on the tenth of November, and talks led by Scott Bessent and He Lifeng now cover AI guardrails and rare-earth magnets as well as tariffs.</s> <s>The truce agreed in Busan capped American tariffs near twenty percent, but a senior US official says Chinese mineral supplies aren't up to par.</s> <s>China refines most of the world's rare earths, and that's the leverage Beijing will carry into Xi Jinping's visit to the White House.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Lagos, auto spare-parts traders protested against foreign suppliers who've started selling directly to customers.</s> <s>Distributive trade employs twenty-seven and a half percent of Nigeria's workforce, and the Centre for the Promotion of Private Enterprise questions whether permit rules are being enforced at all.</s> <s>For millions of Nigerians the market stall has been the first rung out of poverty, and a supplier who turns into a competitor takes that rung away.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Berlin's Left Party won twenty-five point three percent of the vote on a promise to nationalise housing.</s> <s>Its lead candidate, Elif Eralp, wants to move some two hundred and twenty thousand flats into state ownership, carrying out a twenty twenty-one referendum that passed with fifty-eight percent.</s> <s>Tim Kluessendorf of the Social Democrats puts the cost at twenty billion euros, and whether the city can afford that will decide if the referendum ever becomes law.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Typhoon Dujuan has dropped more than three hundred millimetres of rain since Saturday and is closing in on Tokyo.</s> <s>Japan's Meteorological Agency warns that conditions could get worse quickly, because linear rain bands can sit over one narrow strip for hours and raise the risk of flash floods across Kanto.</s> <s>Its landslide warnings are based on how saturated the soil already is, not on rainfall alone... so the danger can peak after the storm has passed.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Theoretical physicist Corentin Laudicina reports that clusters of particles in a cooling liquid stop growing once they reach a limited size.</s> <s>Most liquids crystallise as they cool, but glass keeps a liquid's disorder while it stiffens into a solid, and physicists still don't agree on what stops the flow.</s> <s>People have been making glass for more than four thousand years, and science still can't fully explain how it forms.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A security researcher has found that an OpenAI advertising cookie links ChatGPT accounts to what people do on advertisers' websites.</s> <s>The browser attaches the cookie as soon as an advertiser's page loads OpenAI's script, before any of OpenAI's own code runs, which is the same cross-site tracking that ad-tech pixels use.</s> <s>Put that browsing data next to what people tell a chatbot, and you get a far richer profile than search history ever gave anyone.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>SMEX, a digital rights group based in Beirut, says Arab governments are copying European and Australian bans on children using social media.</s> <s>It points out that those laws rely on courts and data-protection regulators much stronger than most of the region has.</s> <s>By its account, the bans leave algorithmic amplification, the harvesting of children's data and weak platform accountability untouched.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers have built a scheduler for virtual power plants, which pool household batteries and solar panels into one grid resource, and it raised simulated revenue by eighteen percent.</s> <s>According to a manuscript accepted by Nature, it also cut frequency-regulation tracking errors by forty-two percent, using quantum circuits simulated on ordinary computers and public grid data.</s> <s>The authors admit their model ignores decoherence, so the real test on actual quantum hardware is still to come.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>